              trace a change in a document back to the knowledge that might need
              attention.
            </p>
            <p>
              Monitoring could then revisit the original URL and compare its
              main content with the accepted snapshot. Normalising the content
              before comparison filters out differences in formatting. If the
              content has changed, AI reads the difference alongside the linked
              knowledge and assesses its significance. A changed page may
              contain an updated procedure, or the change may have no bearing on
              the guidance already held. Detecting the difference and judging
              its implications require different kinds of work.
            </p>
